{"title":"Career Roadmap · Community Leader","role":"Community Leader","summary":"A Community Leader works with communities to understand needs, coordinate people and programmes, resolve local issues, promote social development and build participation around shared goals.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Level","Education","Category","Degree / Programme","Specialisation","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Undergraduate"},{"text":"Humanities & Social Sciences"},{"text":"BA (General / Honours)"},{"text":"Theology / Religious Studies"},{"text":"Community Leader"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Community Leader works with communities to understand needs, coordinate people and programmes, resolve local issues, promote social development and build participation around shared goals."},{"type":"p","text":"With a BA in Theology / Religious Studies, this pathway can be particularly relevant for community work carried out through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Faith-based organisations"},{"text":"Religious institutions"},{"text":"Charitable organisations"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Social-service organisations"},{"text":"Community-development programmes"},{"text":"Youth organisations"},{"text":"Educational institutions"},{"text":"Interfaith initiatives"},{"text":"Humanitarian organisations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The degree provides knowledge of religious traditions, ethics, philosophy, society, culture and human values. To become professionally employable as a community leader, however, the student should add community development, project management, communication, social research, monitoring & evaluation and digital skills."},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"“Community Leader” is a broad career title rather than a single regulated profession. The exact responsibilities and eligibility depend on the organisation and community context. A theology/religious-studies degree does not automatically confer religious authority or leadership status within a particular faith tradition; where formal religious ordination, certification or denominational recognition is required, that is a separate pathway."}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Aspect","Reality"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree alignment"},{"text":"Good"}],[{"text":"Direct entry"},{"text":"Possible, especially in community/NGO programme roles"}],[{"text":"Leadership experience"},{"text":"Very Important"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Critical"}],[{"text":"Community engagement"},{"text":"Critical"}],[{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Highly valuable"}],[{"text":"Social research"},{"text":"Highly valuable"}],[{"text":"Religious knowledge"},{"text":"Strong foundation"}],[{"text":"PG requirement"},{"text":"Not always required"}],[{"text":"Volunteer experience"},{"text":"Very Important"}],[{"text":"Data/technology"},{"text":"Increasingly useful"}]]}]},{"heading":"What Does a Community Leader Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A community leader may:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Identify community needs"},{"text":"Build relationships with community members"},{"text":"Organise meetings and events"},{"text":"Coordinate volunteers"},{"text":"Develop community programmes"},{"text":"Conduct awareness campaigns"},{"text":"Connect people with services"},{"text":"Support vulnerable groups"},{"text":"Coordinate educational programmes"},{"text":"Organise youth initiatives"},{"text":"Support social-development projects"},{"text":"Work with local institutions"},{"text":"Mediate community concerns"},{"text":"Coordinate fundraising activities"},{"text":"Monitor programme outcomes"},{"text":"Prepare reports"},{"text":"Build partnerships with NGOs and institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the organisation, the role may combine comm